  "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =-24\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-24\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(-24\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (24\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=12$ and $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{3},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 24\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (24\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})) \\\\ 12 & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (24\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}})\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{12}{16} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
